Implemented: double-click empty canvas opens a small pointer-local goal form (title/category/Create/Cancel/More details). Port release and source→actual mouse Shift-click destination→Connect use the same quick connection form with explicit names/IDs/direction/type. More details transfers unsaved fields/type/endpoints/position into the inspector without creating data and marks the transferred draft unsaved. Quick rename and current/target editing preserve other fields and never infer completion. Existing inspector/visible controls remain alternate access.

Right-click or Shift+F10/Context Menu key opens target-specific menus: goal status/rename/counters/grouping/Focus/details; edge type/reverse/confirmed delete/details; selection reviewed bulk actions with exact count/IDs; group rename/collapse/expand/details; empty canvas Create here/Fit/Reset focus. Right-click on selected cards uses the explicit selection; outside goals are labeled single-goal targets even while a selection exists. Single-goal grouping reuses the reviewed bulk dialog with a singleton target scope. No implicit hidden/prerequisite/downstream actions. Menus alone make no roadmap change or discard inspector drafts.

Panels are clamped to the visible browser window and resize safely; keyboard arrows/Home/End navigate menu items, forms submit on Enter, Escape/Cancel discard only the cursor surface, and focus returns predictably to the initiating object/control/viewport. More details focuses the inspector field. Dirty inspector replacement is confirmed only at commit/transfer; declining retains both drafts. Background gestures are temporarily blocked while a cursor modal is open; closing it restores normal pan/selection/move/port gestures. Client-to-world conversion accounts for viewport scrolling as well as zoom/pan for intended creation positions.

Shared model change: `reverseEdge` swaps endpoints on a cloned document and runs existing full validation before any commit. ID/type/other fields are retained. Duplicate pairs, invalid self documents and hard cycles reject atomically. All context edits use existing validated commands/history/autosave; counters remain manual, grouping remains visual, readiness remains canonical and hard-only. No migration; schema/DB version 1, `osrs-ironman-roadmap` / `documents` / `active`, same `http://127.0.0.1:4173/` origin. Cursor drafts/menus never enter saved/exported JSON.

Changed relative to P3-002: `index.html`, `src/main.js`, `src/model/actions.js`, `src/ui/graph.js`, `src/ui/inspector.js`, `src/ui/bulk.js`, `src/style.css`; new `src/ui/cursor.js`. Tests: new `tests/cursor.test.mjs`, `tests/browser_cursor.mjs`, `tests/fixtures/cursor.mjs`; adapted `tests/browser_phase2.mjs` and `tests/browser_bulk.mjs` only where the detailed-inspector regression now needs More details or a scoped cursor Cancel selector. No previous test assertions were removed. Current docs: this handoff, `DECISIONS.md`, `docs/agents/CURRENT_PHASE_GATE.md`, `TEST_REPORT.md`, `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`, `docs/TESTING.md`. Storage, dependency and routing/layout files are unchanged.

