Dependency: pinned, unmodified **elkjs 0.12.0**, bundled locally (1,609,707-byte JS) with upstream license/README, local notice and integrity hashes under `src/vendor/elkjs/`. Declared license **EPL-2.0 OR GPL-3.0-or-later**; this copy uses EPL-2.0. No npm install, package scripts, CDN or external layout runtime. See `src/vendor/elkjs/NOTICE.md`, `integrity.json`, and ADR-017 for provenance/feasibility. HTML/SVG and local storage architecture remain intact.

Phase 3 changes relative to preserved Phase 2: `index.html`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `scripts/build.mjs`, `src/main.js`, `src/model.js`, `src/model/actions.js`, `src/projection.js`, `src/style.css`, `src/ui/graph.js`, `src/ui/inspector.js`; new `src/geometry.js`, `src/navigation.js`, `src/model/groups.js`, `src/layout/elk.js`, `src/layout/routing.js`, `src/layout/metrics.js`, `src/ui/organization.js`, `src/vendor/elkjs/*`, `tests/fixtures/phase3.mjs`, `tests/phase3.test.mjs`, `tests/browser_phase3.mjs`. Updated current docs: this handoff, `DECISIONS.md`, `docs/agents/CURRENT_PHASE_GATE.md`, `README.md`, `PRODUCT_SPEC.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `TEST_REPORT.md`, `docs/TESTING.md`. Phase 2 backup/storage implementation and test files are unchanged. New evidence is separate; no prior evidence or preserved `dist/` was replaced.

Validation on Windows Node **24.22.1**, Chrome **155.0.8059.85**, fresh nonpersistent contexts with real HTTP/IndexedDB: **Pass 59/59 Node tests**, **Pass 12/12 Phase 3 static-build browser scenarios**, **Pass 15/15 existing Phase 1/2 browser regression scenarios**. Separate static output succeeded, includes all source/vendor bytes, rejects an existing output target, performs no external runtime requests, and preserves original `dist/` hashes. See `TEST_REPORT.md` for exact commands/results/Not run limits.

Review package: [static build](evidence/phase3-2026-10-26T19-14-39-604Z/static/index.html), [Phase 3 results](evidence/phase3-2026-10-26T19-14-39-604Z/results.json), [layout metrics](evidence/phase3-2026-10-26T19-14-39-604Z/layout-metrics.json), [Phase 1/2 regression results](evidence/phase2-2026-10-26T19-14-39-938Z/results.json), [Node output](evidence/phase3-validation-2026-10-26/node-tests.txt). `npm run dev` serves current Phase 3 source at the unchanged origin; no install needed. Do not use `npm run preview` for Phase 3: preserved `dist/` is still Phase 1. With the root server running, the separate build is also available at `http://127.0.0.1:4173/evidence/phase3-2026-10-26T19-14-39-604Z/static/`.

Measurements (world px; actual card boxes compact 176×76, detailed 236×108; summary 284×208): seven-goal sample **1715×412 compact / 2015×508 detailed**; 16-goal branching/cyclic/disconnected raid fixture **4029×556 / 4689×700**; collapsed ToA example **2509×696 detailed**. All measured cases: zero card overlap, route-card intersection, label-card/label-label/label-other-edge collision. Initial ELK routes have zero proper crossings; reload routing adds **2 crossings** in the raid fixture in either density. Shared collinear segment incidences are 2 for seven goals, 10 for raid, 4 for collapsed ToA (includes repeated pair incidences; not unique crossings). Each connection retains its own typed selectable label/inspector.

Known defects/limits: **P0/P1 none found in executed checks**. **P2:** two reload/manual-routing crossings on the raid fixture; shared paths can remain visually ambiguous. **P3:** none newly confirmed. Long chains require zoom/pan and Focus; Fit is an overview, not a promise that every label is readable at once. Filter/collapse changes preserve positions, so new summaries or density changes may need explicit Optimize. Arbitrary overlapping manual arrangements are not automatically repaired; route fallback may cross obstacles in such arrangements. Large-graph performance, real quota exhaustion, concurrent tabs, Edge/Firefox/Safari/mobile/accessibility hardening are Not run here and remain outside these measured claims. Main-thread layout performance is not production-accepted.

Owner walkthrough: use disposable data and export personal work first; optimize the demo in both densities, then verify Undo/Redo and a manual move. Create a ToA/Fang/Lightbearer group with different manual states/counters and a representative; collapse, inspect original links, expand and delete (ungroup), then undo. Try completed modes and upstream/downstream/both Focus/Highlight, exit/reset, reload, and JSON roundtrip; positions/state must persist unless moved/optimized. Repeat failed import/save recovery from the Phase 2 checklist. Full steps and runnable test instructions: `README.md`, `docs/TESTING.md`. Next gate: CEO review through Owner, then explicit Owner Phase 3 acceptance. Stop before Phase 4.

